  What Makes This an MVP (and What's Next)
  
  What we built:
  
  - Natural language querying over MDM events
  - Hybrid retrieval (SQL + semantic search)
  - Multi-turn conversations
  - SQL injection protection
  - Containerized deployment
  - Health monitoring via Actuator
  
  What's planned for production hardening:
  
  - Authentication (API key or OAuth2)
  - Rate limiting to control LLM costs
  - Token usage tracking and budgeting
  - Integration tests with Testcontainers
  - Session TTL and eviction policies
  - HTTPS / TLS termination
  - Query cost estimation (reject expensive queries before execution)
  
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  
  Business Value
  
  - Support team can self-serve device investigations — no more waiting for engineering
  - Security analysts can ask "show me failed security updates across all iPhones" in seconds
  - Managers get instant fleet health summaries
  - Engineers stop being interrupted for ad-hoc queries
  
  The MVP proves the concept works. The next phase is hardening it for multi-tenant production use with proper auth, cost controls, and observability.

